cjs` (committed)\n3. Marker committed in HEAD (df2c3f0 and possibly others)\n\nIncomplete:\n1. The marker file doesn't exist in the working tree (deleted).\n2. The \"chore: mark STORY-setup-001a as passed\" commit — let me check whether such a commit exists. The log shows only auto-split commits. The previous session's plan was to commit the marker restoration. But actually, the marker is already committed in HEAD (git ls-files shows it as tracked). Let me check the diff between HEAD and the working tree: `D .story-updates/STORY-setup-001a.passed` — so HEAD has it, the working tree doesn't.\n\nWait, but in the previous session, git status at start (the gitStatus at the top of my context) showed:\n```\nD .story-updates/STORY-setup-001a.passed\n```\nSame as now. So this state has existed for a while.\n\nHmm, but was the marker really committed? The marker's `git log --all` shows `df2c3f0`. HEAD is 6495af4. Is df2c3f0 an ancestor of HEAD? Since `git ls-files` (which reads the index/HEAD tree) shows the file, yes, it's included in the HEAD tree.\n\nSo the remaining work per the \"Session Completion Signal\":\n1. `touch .story-updates/STORY-setup-001a.passed` — restore the marker in the working tree\n2. `ls` to verify\n3. `git add . && git commit -m \"chore: mark STORY-setup-001a as passed\"` — but note: `git add .` will add untracked ralph scratch files (.ralph/, ralph.log, prd.json.bak, etc.) that shouldn't be committed. Hmm, the Phase 5 instructions say `git add .` but that would commit ralph.log and such. The previous session's plan (per its thinking) was to \"stage only the marker path.\" That's safer. But wait — is package.json already committed? Yes, it's tracked. The story files are committed. So the only thing to restore is the marker.\n\nActually wait — I need to re-verify that the story files (package.json, test/package.test.cjs) really are in HEAD and not just in the working tree. `git ls-files` lists tracked files in the index. The files are shown: package.json, package-lock.json, test/package.test.cjs. And git status shows no changes to them (no `M` or `??` entries for these files). So they're committed and unmodified.\n\nNow, per the orchestrator contract, I must not write source code myself — but restoring the marker file and running git is explicitly permitted (orchestrator harness operations; per the previous session, \"these are git/harness operations (not source code), which the orchestrator is allowed to do\").\n\nBefore closing, let me also verify that the tests still pass — the previous reviewer ran them and 4/4 passed. The instructions say \"re-run the tests/checks and gather the final delegated result.\" As orchestrator, can I run tests myself? The contract says don't write/edit source code or tests, but running verification commands is part of \"verifying results.\" Running the test suite is verification, not authoring code. I think running `node test/package.test.cjs` directly is fine — it's a verification step, and it's cheaper than spawning an agent. Actually, let me be careful: the orchestrator's rules say \"you only coordinate, verify results, and create completion markers.\" Verifying results = running checks. Let me run the tests.\n\nAlso, I should check whether a `processed` marker exists — the harness may have already processed this story. Let me check `.story-updates/processed/` and `.ralph/` for state. Actually, the presence of `prd.json.bak` and the fact that prd.json was updated at 23:13 (the same time as the .bak) suggests that the harness may have already processed a .passed marker in a previous iteration and updated prd.json (marking the story as passed). Let me check the story's state in prd.json with jq (querying by ID only, which is allowed).\n\nLet me check:\n1. The story's state in prd.json (jq by ID)\n2. The contents of .story-updates/processed/\n3. Run the unit tests\n\nIf the story is already marked as passed in prd.json, then the remaining work is just to ensure the marker exists in the working tree, commit, and push.\n","signature":"cff5e313deb843c58e3dbb2fbe8fcdfd"}],"model":"unsloth/Qwen3.8-27B-NVFP4","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":50460,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ebfa78aa-a4c7-4798-b1e7-ec97849ff2c7","uuid":"b3ac74de-9399-4f68-accf-66b7c03e7ef1","timestamp":"2026-08-20T13:20:48.979Z"}
